## SDDC Manager API - Create Token Pair (POST /v1/tokens)

SDDC Manager APIs are secured using token-based authentication. As a first step before invocation of any API, an access token has to be obtained.

### How It Works

Invoking the Token API returns a token pair - access token and refresh token. To invoke an API, the access token has to be passed in the Authorization header as a Bearer token.

### API Endpoint Example

The endpoint uses: `curl 'https://sfo-vcf01.rainpole.io/v1/tokens' -i -X POST -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -H 'Accept: application/json' -d '{ "username" : "[email protected]", "password" : "XXXXXXX" }'`

The official documentation is available at: https://developer.broadcom.com/xapis/sddc-manager-api/latest/tokens/

This endpoint requires username and password credentials in the request body and returns both an access token and a refresh token that can be used for subsequent API calls.


